{
  "_comment": [
    "STATUS-jas item 38 step 1: active_document.element_tree, the DOCUMENT's rows for the Layers tree_view.",
    "Order: REVERSE z (topmost first), depth-first. element_selected: at or under a selected path.",
    "name is the element's own name ('' when unnamed; the row template supplies <type_label>).",
    "type is the test-JSON type; type_label is the display label (an equal-radius ellipse is a Circle).",
    "NOT in this first cut, by design: collapse, panel selection, renaming, filters and isolation (the",
    "tree_view widget applies those from its own binds, layers.yaml lp_tree), colours, thumbnails.",
    "The documents are written by the reference codec; the expected rows are authored.",
    "visible_cases (item 38 step 1b): the ROWS TO DRAW, resolved in the core from element_tree and the widget's binds: binds.collapsed (paths), binds.panel_selection (paths), binds.renaming (a path or null). A row under a collapsed CONTAINER is hidden; collapsed is true only on a container; panel_selected and renaming are exact path matches. Expected rows are case 0's authored rows plus the three marks."
  ],
